# Google Drive backup — the OAuth client this build authorises against.
#
# Copy to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in. electron-vite inlines MAIN_VITE_*
# into the main-process bundle at build time, so these are literals in `out/` and a
# rebuild is needed after changing them.
#
# Leaving this file uncopied is fine: the app builds and runs, and Settings then says
# the build carries no client and that connecting is not possible.
#
# One-time setup in Google Cloud:
#   1. Create a project, then enable the Google Drive API.
#   2. OAuth consent screen: External, scope `.../auth/drive.file` only. Publishing to
#      production needs a homepage and a privacy policy on a domain you can verify;
#      staying in Testing works too, but Google then expires refresh tokens after
#      seven days, so you reconnect weekly.
#   3. Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> application type "Desktop app".
#
# No API key and no project number: the backup folder is named rather than browsed to,
# so Google's Picker is not used. Under the `drive.file` scope the app can create and
# reuse a folder of its own, which is all that is needed.
#
# The client secret of a desktop client is not confidential in the usual sense —
# Google's own installed-app documentation says so, and a packaged asar is extractable
# regardless. PKCE is what actually protects the exchange.

MAIN_VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
MAIN_VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
